**6.3.2 Optional Forms of Payment.** You may choose to have your account balance paid in a form other than the normal form described above. The following optional payment forms are available:

- (i) **Lump Sum.** You may elect to receive your account balance in a single lump sum payment. If you are younger than age 55 at the time you receive payment, however, you must deposit the payment (other than your Required Contributions) into an IRA or another employer's qualified retirement plan;
- (ii) **Beneficiary Annuity.** You may elect to receive monthly payments for your life and upon your death have 50%, 75%, or 100% of your benefit paid for the life of any beneficiary you name. The amount of the payment to you will depend upon the percentage of the benefit that will be paid to your named beneficiary, and the ages of you and the beneficiary;
- (iii) **Certain and Continuous Annuity.** Under this form of payment, you will receive monthly payments for your life with a guaranteed minimum number (either 60 or 120) of payments. If you die before receiving the guaranteed number of payments, your designated beneficiary will receive the remaining payments.

8.7 The Pension Committee shall have such powers as may be necessary to discharge its duties hereunder. In addition to any implied powers and duties which may be needed to carry out the provisions of the Plan, the Pension Committee shall have the following specific powers and duties:

(A) To adopt bylaws and to make and enforce such rules and regulations as it shall deem necessary or proper for the efficient administration of the Plan and the conduct and transaction of its business affairs;

(B) To interpret and construe the Plan and to decide any and all matters arising hereunder, including the right to remedy possible ambiguities, inconsistencies or omissions; provided, however, that all such interpretation and decisions shall be applied in a uniform manner to all Employees similarly situated;

(C) To determine all questions of eligibility for benefits and to compute the amount of benefits which shall be payable to any Participant or Beneficiary in accordance with the provisions of the Plan;

(D) To authorize payment of benefits from the Trustee (any instructions of the Pension Committee to the Trustee shall be evidenced in writing and signed by such Committee or the person authorized or delegated with such authority in accordance with Section 8.10);

(E) To employ such advisors (including, but not limited to, attorneys, independent public accountants, and actuaries but excluding investment advisors and Trustees) and such other technical and clerical personnel as may be required in the Pension Committee's discretion for the proper administration of the Plan; and

(F) To establish reasonable procedures for determining the qualified status of domestic relations orders which relate to the Plan, as provided in Section 414(p) of the Code.
